course: dictionary
lesson: 2570
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A delta forms where a river drops its sediment at the mouth faster than the sea can carry it away.» The river, the mouth and the sea are clues: this delta is a place on land, not a letter or a sum.
explain: Now look at «The Ganges is sacred to Hindus, and together with the Brahmaputra it forms the largest river delta in the world.» The word river tells you which meaning to use. If the sentence had talked about a letter or a change in a number, you would pick a different meaning. Always ask: what does the sentence around this word tell me about it?
explain: Check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence. A delta is flat land built from mud and sand, so «The delta is home to hundreds of kinds of birds, fish and frogs» makes sense. A delta is a place where animals live, so the sentence is true.
fact: A delta is flat land where a river splits into many smaller streams before it flows into the sea.
fact: Deltas are made from mud and sand that the river carries and drops as it slows down.
fact: «Delta» is also the fourth letter of the Greek alphabet, written Δ or δ.
fact: In maths and science, Δ stands for a change in an amount.
fact: Deltas can be good for farming because the soil is rich, but they can flood easily.
exercise: «A delta is flat land built from the mud and sand a river drops where it slows down at its mouth.» What is a delta? | A steep mountain with snow on top | A very fast river | *Flat land built from mud and sand where a river slows down at its mouth | A deep lake in the middle of a forest
exercise: In maths and science, what does the symbol Δ stand for? | The first letter of the alphabet | A river and its mouth | *A change in an amount | The sea and the land beside it
exercise: «Floods spread mud on flat land beside the river, making a fertile flood plain.» Find and copy one word that means good for growing crops. | mud | flood | beside | *fertile
test: Where does a river split into smaller streams before it flows into the sea? | Inside a cave | *At the delta, near the sea | Under a bridge | In its source high in the mountains
test: «The Ganges and the Brahmaputra form the largest river delta in the world, most of it in Bangladesh.» Which country is most of it in? | *Bangladesh | India | Egypt | Australia
exam: Why do deltas form at the mouth of a river? | Because the sea pushes the river uphill | Because the mud is made of stone | *Because the river slows down and drops its mud and sand | Because the river runs faster there and washes everything away
